  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 1.84,
      "end": 32.68,
      "text": "This is Tommy Vance on Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.85,
      "end": 49.85,
      "text": "From the archives",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 452.52,
      "end": 453.56,
      "text": "put together in the studios",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 453.56,
      "end": 455.2,
      "text": "of the BBC in April 1965,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 455.56,
      "end": 456.48,
      "text": "that was John Mayall,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 456.56,
      "end": 457.08,
      "text": "and as I said,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 457.12,
      "end": 458.22,
      "text": "to the best of our knowledge,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 458.38,
      "end": 460.24,
      "text": "Mr. Clapton was on the guitar.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 462.64,
      "end": 463.34,
      "text": "Three tracks you heard,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 463.42,
      "end": 463.96,
      "text": "the first one was",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 463.96,
      "end": 464.66,
      "text": "Crawling Up a Hill,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 464.82,
      "end": 466.14,
      "text": "the second, Crocodile Walk,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 466.2,
      "end": 467.38,
      "text": "and then last one",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 467.38,
      "end": 468.34,
      "text": "was Bye Bye Bird,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 468.4,
      "end": 469.18,
      "text": "and there's a great version",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 469.18,
      "end": 469.72,
      "text": "of that song,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 469.72,
      "end": 472.2,
      "text": "Bye Bye Bird on the Moody Blues first LP.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 472.76,
      "end": 474.66,
      "text": "Also recorded, I think, around about 1965,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 474.92,
      "end": 477.66,
      "text": "back in the days when it incorporated Mr. Denny Lane.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 477.92,
      "end": 479.42,
      "text": "More from John Mayall later.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 482.72,
      "end": 484.92,
      "text": "Saxon are going to be on Rock on Saturday tomorrow.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 485.08,
      "end": 486.7,
      "text": "They're also on the Friday Rock Show.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 540.0,
      "end": 895.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 900.0,
      "end": 1134.46,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1134.46,
      "end": 1135.86,
      "text": "And that's something that band could record",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1135.86,
      "end": 1138.8,
      "text": "the telephone directory of any town or city in the world,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1138.86,
      "end": 1139.58,
      "text": "and I'd like it.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1139.64,
      "end": 1140.64,
      "text": "They're such a good band.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1140.7,
      "end": 1141.72,
      "text": "Whoever's in the band.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1142.48,
      "end": 1144.4,
      "text": "Because they change every once in a while, don't they?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1144.68,
      "end": 1146.88,
      "text": "Have us hawk wind on a track from their new album.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1146.88,
      "end": 1148.06,
      "text": "The album's called Levitation.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1148.52,
      "end": 1149.9,
      "text": "The track was Motorway City.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1152.36,
      "end": 1153.8,
      "text": "Played a bit of Hawkwind for loads of people,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1153.88,
      "end": 1157.32,
      "text": "including Mark and Robin and Tony and Adrian and Ian and Simon and Philip and Joanne",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1157.32,
      "end": 1160.38,
      "text": "and Kate and Claire and Liz and Jane and everybody else who went to the Isle of Wight camp.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1160.96,
      "end": 1163.92,
      "text": "Also, Toby, Windy, Pete, Amish, Mobbin.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1164.54,
      "end": 1165.36,
      "text": "Can't read the next one.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1165.42,
      "end": 1166.68,
      "text": "It could be Phyllis or Phoebe.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1166.68,
      "end": 1170.98,
      "text": "And all the other cranium crushers of William Parker, Upper Sixth in Hastings.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1171.44,
      "end": 1174.42,
      "text": "Thank you, says Gonzo and Rudolph the Red-Nosed Werewolf.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1175.24,
      "end": 1179.1,
      "text": "Also, Hawkwind was for Baz and Fraz and Arthur.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1179.88,
      "end": 1183.16,
      "text": "And all the good mates who go to the YF in Cheadle.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1183.38,
      "end": 1187.4,
      "text": "Good wishes for Nigel Fleming, who lives, what do you believe, in Cheadle?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1188.16,
      "end": 1192.44,
      "text": "Hawken was also for a lady by the name of Elizabeth McCall, a good friend of John Cooper.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1192.66,
      "end": 1193.84,
      "text": "John lives in Glasgow.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1195.07,
      "end": 1198.53,
      "text": "Hawtwin, too, was for Hugh and for Goyne, or possibly Gwyn and for Phil,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1198.77,
      "end": 1200.67,
      "text": "and for Paul and Mark and Ian and Alistair.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1201.05,
      "end": 1202.43,
      "text": "I sound like a telephone director.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1202.95,
      "end": 1205.89,
      "text": "And Dave and Wendy and Nick and Moy and Adam from Brecon.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1206.61,
      "end": 1210.15,
      "text": "And finally, for everybody who goes to Dunsmore School in rugby.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1210.73,
      "end": 1213.63,
      "text": "And before that, you heard something from the new album by Motor.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1213.75,
      "end": 1214.85,
      "text": "I beg your pardon, by Saxon.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1214.89,
      "end": 1216.25,
      "text": "The album's called Strong Arm of the Law.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1216.69,
      "end": 1218.03,
      "text": "The track was Taking Your Chances,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1218.37,
      "end": 1220.37,
      "text": "and that was for all the good friends of Mr David Crook,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1221.01,
      "end": 1227.74,
      "text": "whom I'm absolutely sure isn't.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1227.86,
      "end": 1229.78,
      "text": "It's just about 16 minutes to 11.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1229.92,
      "end": 1232.22,
      "text": "Here's a new band you've probably never heard of before.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1232.68,
      "end": 1235.14,
      "text": "They were formed in 1975 in Sunderland.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1235.3,
      "end": 1236.14,
      "text": "They now live in London.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1236.26,
      "end": 1237.36,
      "text": "They've been here for three years.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1237.8,
      "end": 1238.38,
      "text": "Give them a chance.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1238.48,
      "end": 1239.46,
      "text": "They're called Hibiscus.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1240.06,
      "end": 1247.26,
      "text": "Bit of a classic by Rush from the album Hemispheres, The Trees.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1247.26,
      "end": 1615.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1620.0,
      "end": 1918.39,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1918.39,
      "end": 1919.71,
      "text": "For all the Rush freaks around the country,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1919.87,
      "end": 1921.35,
      "text": "and good heavens, aren't there a lot of them,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1921.47,
      "end": 1924.27,
      "text": "including Tony Hughes and everybody at the Green Garage in Abertillery.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1925.3,
      "end": 1926.58,
      "text": "And Abertillery, isn't it?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1926.82,
      "end": 1928.56,
      "text": "Well, you know where it is, in Wales.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1929.89,
      "end": 1933.75,
      "text": "For Dave and Rich and Mark and Ray from Chelmsley Wood.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1934.49,
      "end": 1938.79,
      "text": "And for Andy and all his friends who live in Scotland.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1939.84,
      "end": 1941.68,
      "text": "And lots of love to Tracy from Neil Reid.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1942.46,
      "end": 1947.12,
      "text": "I'll also for Bod and Fletch and Mike and Matty the Welshman and Stakes the Hare, I think it is.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1947.24,
      "end": 1949.22,
      "text": "They all go to the Kingswood School in Bath.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1949.96,
      "end": 1952.68,
      "text": "And before that, the first of three from a new band by the name of Hibiscus.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1952.86,
      "end": 1954.86,
      "text": "The track you heard was called White Night.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1958.79,
      "end": 1961.49,
      "text": "Four minutes to eleven, it's time for the Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1961.75,
      "end": 1963.35,
      "text": "The last one on the air was a fortnight ago.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1963.35,
      "end": 1967.93,
      "text": "We played you the Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse track by Aphrodite's Child.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1968.05,
      "end": 1969.81,
      "text": "Then we played you a track from Quadrophenia.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1969.97,
      "end": 1972.01,
      "text": "And we played you something from Sab's Volume 4.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1972.73,
      "end": 1974.33,
      "text": "Just about everybody got the answer right.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1974.33,
      "end": 1978.97,
      "text": "In fact, I think something like 99.999% recurring.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1979.73,
      "end": 1981.17,
      "text": "The answer, of course, was four.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1981.47,
      "end": 1984.77,
      "text": "Four Horsemen, Quadrovina, and Sabs Volume 4.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1985.49,
      "end": 1989.0,
      "text": "But the person that gets the £10 record token is Mr. Phil Saunders,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1989.12,
      "end": 1992.9,
      "text": "who lives at [redacted address], St. Giles Estate, Whitchurch in Bristol.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1995.75,
      "end": 1997.63,
      "text": "So, Phil, you get yourself a £10 record token.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1997.71,
      "end": 2000.41,
      "text": "That will be in the post just as soon as I can raise the money out of Tony Wilson.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2000.49,
      "end": 2004.51,
      "text": "You know how hard it is, and it gets progressively more difficult as we stay on the air.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2004.51,
      "end": 2007.73,
      "text": "and you've put together a really tasty Friday Night Connection yourself.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2008.27,
      "end": 2011.71,
      "text": "And here it is, three bits of music within which there is a theme.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2012.71,
      "end": 2017.51,
      "text": "And that's our Friday Night Connection for tonight.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2017.51,
      "end": 2874.7,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2874.7,
      "end": 2881.25,
      "text": "It is, of course, three bits of music with a theme or connection contained therein,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2881.43,
      "end": 2882.63,
      "text": "intertwined within.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2884.04,
      "end": 2888.72,
      "text": "Put together by Mr. Phil Saunders of 19 Woodcombe St. Giles Estate Woodchurch in Bristol,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2888.82,
      "end": 2889.84,
      "text": "if you think you know what it is.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2889.94,
      "end": 2892.14,
      "text": "And it's pretty, pretty simple, really.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2892.84,
      "end": 2895.36,
      "text": "Jot down your answer on a postcard, letter,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2895.54,
      "end": 2897.58,
      "text": "any form of communication you like, and send it to",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2897.58,
      "end": 2899.32,
      "text": "The Friday Night Connection,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2899.8,
      "end": 2902.46,
      "text": "The Friday Rock Show, BBC Radio 1,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2902.82,
      "end": 2905.08,
      "text": "London, W1A, 4WW.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2905.88,
      "end": 2908.39,
      "text": "And if yours is the first card we pull out of the bag,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2908.45,
      "end": 2909.71,
      "text": "the one that we find most attractive,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2909.83,
      "end": 2911.01,
      "text": "with, of course, the correct answer,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2911.61,
      "end": 2913.47,
      "text": "then you'll get yourself a £10 record token.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2913.89,
      "end": 2914.91,
      "text": "The best of luck.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2915.29,
      "end": 2925.46,
      "text": "The Friday Rock Show from BBC Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2925.46,
      "end": 2927.28,
      "text": "It's 11 minutes after 11.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2927.46,
      "end": 2929.9,
      "text": "Sorry about the lack of personal mentions tonight",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2929.9,
      "end": 2934.26,
      "text": "for all the people that I met at the Birmingham football match last Sunday.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2934.36,
      "end": 2937.38,
      "text": "Unfortunately, I left the bits of paper at home on a shelf,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2937.56,
      "end": 2939.58,
      "text": "but I'll dig them out and play them next week.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2940.1,
      "end": 2943.12,
      "text": "Meanwhile, for all of you, here's Hibiscus and I See the Sun.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2943.6,
      "end": 2954.4,
      "text": "I'm in Southampton on the 20th, or rather I should say the 2nd of October in this year.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3739.35,
      "end": 3743.89,
      "text": "That, of course, is the live version of Mr Crowley by Ozzy Osbourne's Blizzard of Ours,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3744.31,
      "end": 3748.71,
      "text": "and it was released today, and I played it specially today for a gentleman who had a birthday yesterday.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3749.29,
      "end": 3751.59,
      "text": "I think he was 20, and he's feeling a bit depressed",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3751.59,
      "end": 3753.13,
      "text": "because he thinks he's past it all.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3753.29,
      "end": 3754.15,
      "text": "I doubt it very much.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3754.47,
      "end": 3755.13,
      "text": "His name is Duncan.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3755.57,
      "end": 3757.21,
      "text": "Best wishes from his sister.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3757.65,
      "end": 3760.77,
      "text": "His sister's name is Pauline, and they live in Croydon in Surrey.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3760.99,
      "end": 3762.85,
      "text": "And prior to that, you heard Hibiscus,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3763.39,
      "end": 3766.15,
      "text": "and a track which is called I See the Sun.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3766.65,
      "end": 3766.93,
      "text": "Where?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3766.93,
      "end": 3775.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3805.66,
      "end": 3810.46,
      "text": "...from an album that came out in 1978,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3810.46,
      "end": 4234.93,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4238.57,
      "end": 4239.93,
      "text": "the album called Taken by Force.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4239.93,
      "end": 4242.41,
      "text": "The track was He's a Woman, She's a Man.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4243.37,
      "end": 4245.47,
      "text": "And that was for a gentleman by the name of Robin,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4245.59,
      "end": 4246.81,
      "text": "Morrison Smith",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4246.81,
      "end": 4248.26,
      "text": "It seems",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4248.26,
      "end": 4249.12,
      "text": "It sums him up",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4249.12,
      "end": 4249.8,
      "text": "Beautifully",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4249.8,
      "end": 4250.82,
      "text": "But I didn't write that",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4250.82,
      "end": 4251.42,
      "text": "Somebody else did",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4251.42,
      "end": 4252.2,
      "text": "It's rather anonymous",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4252.2,
      "end": 4253.3,
      "text": "But obviously",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4253.3,
      "end": 4254.34,
      "text": "Somebody who knows him well",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4254.34,
      "end": 4256.32,
      "text": "Also played the Scorpions",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4256.32,
      "end": 4257.52,
      "text": "For Mark Jarvis",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4257.52,
      "end": 4258.82,
      "text": "And all his mates",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4258.82,
      "end": 4259.9,
      "text": "Who live in Amberley",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4259.9,
      "end": 4260.88,
      "text": "In Gloucestershire",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4260.88,
      "end": 4262.02,
      "text": "And prior to that",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4262.02,
      "end": 4262.98,
      "text": "You heard Thin Lizzy",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4262.98,
      "end": 4264.08,
      "text": "Live and Dangerous",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4264.08,
      "end": 4264.58,
      "text": "Was the album",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4264.58,
      "end": 4265.64,
      "text": "The track was Emerald",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4265.64,
      "end": 4266.82,
      "text": "And that was for",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4266.82,
      "end": 4267.54,
      "text": "Stan and Alice",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4267.54,
      "end": 4268.34,
      "text": "And Coxie and Smithy",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4268.34,
      "end": 4269.3,
      "text": "And Ian and Gav",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4269.3,
      "end": 4270.28,
      "text": "And everybody else",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4270.28,
      "end": 4271.8,
      "text": "Best wishes from G Hilton",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4271.8,
      "end": 4273.3,
      "text": "Also very best wishes",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4273.3,
      "end": 4274.04,
      "text": "To a load of people",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4274.04,
      "end": 4275.0,
      "text": "Who are at the moment",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4275.0,
      "end": 4277.66,
      "text": "involved in the 36-hour table tennis marathon",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4277.66,
      "end": 4280.3,
      "text": "in Rishton in Blackburn.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4280.82,
      "end": 4283.16,
      "text": "They're all members of the Rishton Scout Group.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4283.56,
      "end": 4286.68,
      "text": "That's Adam and Timmy and Martin and Carl and Michael.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4286.9,
      "end": 4288.26,
      "text": "Keep on batting that ball.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4293.08,
      "end": 4294.74,
      "text": "It's 26 and a half minutes to midnight.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4294.92,
      "end": 4295.8,
      "text": "Back into the archives.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4296.02,
      "end": 4298.58,
      "text": "Now we go back to 1967 for more John Mayall.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4298.58,
      "end": 4734.4,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4734.4,
      "end": 4736.22,
      "text": "if you were listening to the light program",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4736.22,
      "end": 4739.34,
      "text": "as it was in those days in, what, January 1967,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4739.34,
      "end": 4741.58,
      "text": "You would have heard that the first time it went out.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4741.68,
      "end": 4743.04,
      "text": "Three numbers by John Mayall.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4743.34,
      "end": 4744.92,
      "text": "Leapin' Christine was the last one.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4745.34,
      "end": 4746.42,
      "text": "Before that, Sittin' in the Rain.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4746.64,
      "end": 4749.6,
      "text": "And prior to that, Riding on the L and N.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4749.94,
      "end": 4751.42,
      "text": "John Anderson's got a new album out.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4751.7,
      "end": 4752.7,
      "text": "Here's a track from it.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5040.0,
      "end": 5382.5,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5382.5,
      "end": 5383.44,
      "text": "Absolute magic.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5383.82,
      "end": 5387.22,
      "text": "From the new double album that's just come out called Eagles Live, The Eagles There,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5387.4,
      "end": 5389.34,
      "text": "and a live version of Hotel California.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5389.92,
      "end": 5392.22,
      "text": "And before that, something from the brand new album by John Anderson.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5392.44,
      "end": 5393.12,
      "text": "It's a good one.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5393.18,
      "end": 5394.14,
      "text": "It's called Song of Seven.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5394.2,
      "end": 5396.12,
      "text": "The track was For You, For Me.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5396.66,
      "end": 5399.18,
      "text": "And now we're going to play our last from Bob Corner,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5399.3,
      "end": 5401.16,
      "text": "who plays the keyboards, Graham Close on the guitar,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5401.36,
      "end": 5404.18,
      "text": "Kevin Moore on the bass, and Pete Saunders on the drums.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5404.52,
      "end": 5408.98,
      "text": "The four gentlemen who came down from Sunderland some three years ago",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5408.98,
      "end": 5411.5,
      "text": "down to London, and they're trying to get a recording deal",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5411.5,
      "end": 5412.62,
      "text": "and also a publishing deal.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5412.72,
      "end": 5415.1,
      "text": "So if anybody's interested, after they hear this,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5415.26,
      "end": 5418.02,
      "text": "well, write to us and we'll let you know where to find Hibiscus.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5418.02,
      "end": 5419.88,
      "text": "This is called Quilter.",
      "source": "TV"
    }
  ]
}